{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["With blindness — a plague of blinding and desolation." "וַיִּלְאוּ — its meaning is: they could no longer find the entrance. They did not seek the entrance. And likewise: וְנִלְאוּ מִצְרַיִם לִשְׁתּוֹת מַיִם מִן הַיְאֹר — they could not drink, since it was blood. And so it proves at the end: וְלֹא יָכְלוּ לִשְׁתּוֹת מִמֵּימֵי הַיְאֹר. And in several places the form נלאו is doubled, as in: ״[נלאיתי] כלכל לא אוכל״. And likewise: ״והיה כי נראה כי נלאה מואב אל הבמות ובא אל מקדשו להתפלל ולא יוכל״. And likewise: ״הנסה דבר אליך תלאה ועצור במילין מי יוכל״ — that is: because the Holy One, blessed be He, tested you with afflictions, you grow weary — that is, you are unable to remain silent, and you thought in your heart and said: ועצור במילין מי יוכל."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {1 "The last biblical quotation appears to be from Daniel 7:19 with significant variation from the received text; translated hyper-literally as it stands in the manuscript."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:37.902856834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}